# data file for fldtk fluid (Fast Light User Interface Designer)
version 1.0000
comment {The Grid sub-panel of widget_panel.fl's own widget_tabs -- shown in
place of the ordinary GUI/Style/C++ tabs when the selected widget is a
Fl_Grid (GridNode). Ported from FLTK's fluid/panels/
widget_panel/Grid_Tab.fl.

Named `widget_panel_grid_tab.fl` rather than `GridTab.fl` (the name
its own `widget_class GridTab` would suggest) so this file groups with
`widget_panel.fl` in a directory listing; `widget_panel.fl`'s own
top-level `decl` block imports this file's class explicitly, since its
file name doesn't match its class name.

Unlike FLTK (which reaches into the live project tree itself via a
static `Grid_Node::selected()` lookup, fully decoupled from
widget_panel.cxx), this file has no live-canvas-widget access yet (the
same standing simplification the rest of widget_panel.fl's own
GUI/Style/C++ pass already established) -- `GridTab` instead exposes a
real public `load(GridNode gn)` method that widget_panel.fl's own
`propagateLoadWidget()` calls directly when the selection is a
GridNode, matching the same `currentXNode_`/`propagateLoadX()` shape
every other page in that file already uses, just scoped to this
class's own field instead of a module-level global. Every field reads
and writes `GridNode`'s own already-real data fields (`rows`/`cols`/
`marginLeft`-`marginBottom`/`gapRow`/`gapCol`/`rowHeights`/
`rowWeights`/`rowGaps`/`colWidths`/`colWeights`/`colGaps`) -- no live
`Fl_Grid` query, matching that same simplification.}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
decl {import fluid;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
widget_class GridTab
  {
    xywh {0 0 400 330}
    labelsize 11
    resizable
    position_relative_rescale
  }
  {
    decl {private GridNode gn_;}
      {
        private
        local
      }
    Group {}
      {
        label {Grid Layout:}
        xywh {85 30 315 20}
        labelfont 1
        labelsize 11
        align 4
      }
      {
        Input widgetGridRows
          {
            label {Rows:}
            callback {if (gn_ is null) return;
int m;
try m = to!int(widgetGridRows.value()); catch (ConvException) m = 0;
if (m < 1)
  \{
    m = 1;
    widgetGridRows.value("1");
  \}
gn_.rows = m;
gn_.hasDimensions = true;
load(gn_);}
            xywh {85 30 40 20}
            labelsize 11
            textsize 11
            align 5
            tooltip {Number of horizontal rows in the Grid group}
          }
        Group {}
          {
            xywh {125 30 30 20}
          }
          {
            Button {}
              {
                label {−}
                callback {int m;
try m = to!int(widgetGridRows.value()); catch (ConvException) m = 0;
widgetGridRows.value(to!string(m - 1));
widgetGridRows.doCallback();}
                xywh {125 30 15 20}
                labelsize 11
                compact {1}
                setup {o.clearVisibleFocus();}
              }
            Button {}
              {
                label {+}
